    {
      "id": "nda-exception-source-development-evidence",
      "hypothesis_ids": [
        "nda-12",
        "nda-13"
      ],
      "guidance": {
        "inspection": "Keep independent development and third-party acquisition analytically separate. Development is supported by an operative exclusion or right covering information developed independently, normally qualified by no access to, reference to, or use of protected information and sometimes by contemporaneous proof. Prior possession or creation before disclosure is not the same as later independent development. Third-party acquisition requires an operative exclusion or permission tied to a source other than the discloser, usually conditioned on lawful receipt, a nonconfidential basis, and the source’s lack of a confidentiality duty. An “independently acquired or developed” formulation may address both, but a mere acknowledgment that similar information may be received from others is not necessarily permission. Do not transfer a development qualification to the third-party task or vice versa. Read the exception preamble with the item and preserve provenance, timing, knowledge, access, proof, and confidentiality qualifications. Search the full exclusions and any separate independent-development section when the returned fragment is incomplete.",
