        "inspection": "For each task, identify an operative permission to disclose or grant access, then resolve the permitted class. Employee sharing requires that the receiving party’s employees are within that class; third-party sharing requires nonemployees such as agents, contractors, consultants, counsel, accountants, advisers, financing sources, or other representatives. A representative definition is useful only when connected to an operative disclosure or access clause. Preserve need-to-know, stated-purpose, confidentiality-undertaking, consent, and responsibility conditions. Do not treat a clause merely naming representatives, the disclosing party’s personnel, solicitation targets, or persons receiving information from the recipient as authorization. An employee-only exception to a general nondisclosure rule may support employee sharing while opposing broader third-party sharing; a broad representative permission can support both only if its definition actually contains both classes. Read cross-referenced definitions and the complete disclosure clause, especially where the permission and recipient list appear in different provisions.",
