        "inspection": "Start from the operative restriction, not an exception containing the word “solicitation.” For the exact hypothesis, determine whether the receiving party or its affiliates or representatives are barred from soliciting for hire, employing, recruiting, or initiating employment contact with officers, employees, or other personnel of the disclosing party. Follow the clause through all enumerated target classes, duration, consent or approval requirements, contact-based limitations, and exceptions for unsolicited approaches, former employees, general advertising, or nonspecific recruiters. Such exceptions narrow the prohibition; they do not reverse it. Proxy solicitation and standstill provisions are a distinct mechanism: retain them when independently operative and responsive to the broader evidence request, but do not use proxy language alone as a substitute for a personnel or representative target. Headings, definitions, and carve-outs without their parent prohibition are insufficient. Inspect adjacent list items and the complete section whenever a query lands only on an exception.",
